          "text": "China Reduces Academic Burden on Students\n\nThe Chinese Ministry of Education has announced a series of measures aimed at improving students' physical and mental health.\n\nThese measures include banning excessive homework, frequent testing, and encroachment on students' break time.\n\nThe new rules also prohibit kindergartens from introducing the curriculum too early and require schools to conduct entrance exams for students.\n\nThis initiative is part of the authorities' policy to reduce academic pressure on children, which experts believe leads to sleep deprivation, anxiety, and depression.\n\nIn November 2025, regulators already mandated that schools monitor the amount of homework and ensure students get at least two hours of physical activity daily."
